module eclDetection

manifest MagneticParticles
manifest TargetSequence
manifest HybridizationBuffer
manifest RuPhen3Cl2
manifest PBS
manifest TPA
manifest PluronicF68

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Electrochemiluminescence on Digital Microfluidics for
// microRNA Analysis
// Shamsi, Choi, Ng, Chamberlain, Wheeler
// Biosensors and Bioelectronics, 2015
// DOI: 10.1016/j.bios.2015.10.036
//
// Protocol: Magnetic particle-based oligonucleotide
// hybridization assay on DMF coupled to ECL detection.
// miRNA-143 (ds-143) is captured by ss-143-modified
// Dynabeads M-280 Streptavidin and detected via
// [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2 intercalation and TPA co-reactant
// at ITO working electrodes on the DMF top-plate.
//
// REAGENT NOTES:
//   MagneticParticles: 4.5 uL aliquots of Dynabeads M-280
//     Streptavidin (10 mg/mL, ~6-7e8 particles/mL in PBS,
//     0.1% BSA, 0.02% NaN3) pre-coated with ss-143 probe
//     DNA via avidin-biotin chemistry. All solutions
//     supplemented with 0.05% Pluronics F68 v/v.
//   TargetSequence: ds-143 in hybridization buffer (0, 10,
//     100, or 1000 nM). For cell lysate assays, MCF-7 or
//     MDA-MB-231 lysate diluted 1:10 in sample dilution
//     buffer (pH 8.0, Tris-base 7.7 mM, Tris-HCl 12.2 mM,
//     NaCl 200 mM, MgCl2 5 mM, BSA 4% w/v, Pluronic L64
//     0.05% w/v).
//   HybridizationBuffer: 20 mM Tris-HCl, 0.2 M NaCl,
//     5 mM MgCl2, pH 8.0.
//   RuPhen3Cl2: 200 uM [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2 in PBS (1x), pH 7.5.
//   PBS: phosphate buffered saline (1x), pH 7.5.
//   TPA: 20 mM tripropylamine in PBS (1x), pH 7.5.
//   PluronicF68: 0.05% v/v in all above solutions.
//
// ECL DETECTION NOTE:
//   eclDetection module abstracts the ITO working electrode
//   (WE, 800 um dia.) and Ag/Au/ITO counter/pseudoreference
//   (CE/RE, 560 um x 560 um) on the DMF top-plate. 1.5 V
//   DC applied for 45 s; maximum ECL photon count recorded
//   within the first 10 s via PMT (CV ~10%).
//   Ru(Phen)3(2+) intercalates dsDNA (4 bp per ion); signal
//   is proportional to hybridized ds-143 captured on beads.
//   LOD: 1.1 nM (CLOD), 1.5 femtomoles (absolute). Total
//   assay time: ~40 min for two parallel assays.
//
// MAGNETIC SEPARATION NOTE:
//   All `heat` steps marked "magnet" abstract the permanent
//   magnet positioned below the DMF bottom plate to
//   immobilize Dynabeads while the supernatant droplet is
//   transported away by electrode actuation. The temperature
//   parameter (25c) reflects ambient/room temperature;
//   no thermal effect is intended at these steps.
//
// PRE-ASSAY STEP (off-chip, not encoded in BioScript):
//   Cathodic electrochemical cleaning of ITO WEs:
//   cyclic voltammetry in 20 uL PBS (1x) on DMF top-plate,
//   10 cycles from -1 V to 0 V at 100 mV/s using ITO WE
//   and Ag/Au/ITO CE/RE.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: particle dispense and
//                             magnetic separation; target
//                             hybridization; wash x4;
//                             Ru(Phen)3 labeling; wash x2;
//                             TPA addition; ECL detection
//   BB2  eclPass           -- eclSignal > 0: valid ECL above
//                             blank; dispose final droplet
//   BB3  eclFail           -- eclSignal <= 0: no signal
//                             (below LOD or reagent failure);
//                             drain final droplet
//   BB4  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose ECL signal
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Dispense magnetic particle droplets and merge.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "three unit droplets containing
//   magnetic particles were dispensed from their reservoir
//   and merged." (For cell lysate assays, five unit droplets
//   were used instead of three; three used here for the
//   standard synthetic target protocol.)
//   Each unit droplet ~1.8 uL; three merged = ~5.4 uL total.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beads1 = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
beads2 = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
beads3 = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles

beadsMerge1 = mix beads1 with beads2 for 5s
beadsMerged = mix beadsMerge1 with beads3 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Magnetic separation - pellet beads, remove
//   supernatant (storage buffer). Magnet applied below device;
//   supernatant droplet actuated away from bead pellet.
//   `heat` at 25c for 30s abstracts magnet hold time.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat beadsMerged at 25c for 30s
dispose beadsMerged

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Dispense target sequence droplets and merge.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "two unit droplets of target sequence
//   solution were dispensed, merged, and delivered to the
//   immobilized particles for resuspension and incubation
//   for 15 min."
//   TargetSequence reservoir: ds-143 in hybridization buffer
//   at test concentration (10/100/1000 nM) or cell lysate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

target1 = dispense 1 units of TargetSequence
target2 = dispense 1 units of TargetSequence

targetMerged = mix target1 with target2 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Hybridization incubation.
//   Deliver merged target droplet to bead pellet; resuspend
//   by electrode actuation (mixing) and incubate for 15 min.
//   ds-143 hybridizes to ss-143 immobilized on beads.
//   `mix` abstracts both resuspension and incubation; the
//   15m duration encodes the hybridization dwell time.
//
//   NOTE: beadsMerged was disposed after magnetic separation
//   (step 2). The bead pellet physically remains on-device
//   at the electrode; targetMerged is merged with a freshly
//   dispensed bead pellet representation. In BioScript,
//   re-dispense from MagneticParticles models the pellet
//   being resuspended by the incoming target droplet, which
//   is the physical reality of the protocol (the magnet is
//   removed and electrode actuation drives resuspension).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pelletForHybrid = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
hybridDroplet   = mix pelletForHybrid with targetMerged for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Magnetic separation - remove unbound target.
//   Magnet applied; beads pellet; supernatant (unbound ds-143)
//   actuated away. `heat` at 25c for 30s = magnet hold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat hybridDroplet at 25c for 30s
dispose hybridDroplet

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Wash cycle x4 (hybridization buffer).
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "particles were washed four times in
//   series by re-suspending and mixing with one unit droplet
//   of hybridization buffer followed by magnetic separation
//   from the supernatant."
//   Each wash: dispense 1 unit HybridizationBuffer, mix 1m
//   to resuspend beads, apply magnet 30s, dispose supernatant.
//   Four serial wash cycles encoded explicitly below.
//
//   As in STEP 4, pellet re-dispense from MagneticParticles
//   models the retained bead pellet at each wash cycle.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Wash 1
pelletW1   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf1   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix1   = mix pelletW1 with washBuf1 for 1m
heat washMix1 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix1

// Wash 2
pelletW2   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf2   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix2   = mix pelletW2 with washBuf2 for 1m
heat washMix2 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix2

// Wash 3
pelletW3   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf3   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix3   = mix pelletW3 with washBuf3 for 1m
heat washMix3 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix3

// Wash 4
pelletW4   = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
washBuf4   = dispense 1 units of HybridizationBuffer
washMix4   = mix pelletW4 with washBuf4 for 1m
heat washMix4 at 25c for 30s
dispose washMix4

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2 intercalation labeling.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "two unit droplets of [Ru(Phen)3]Cl2
//   solution were dispensed, merged, and delivered to the
//   particles, where they were re-suspended and mixed for
//   2 min. The particles were then separated from the
//   supernatant droplet."
//   Ru(Phen)3(2+) intercalates into dsDNA (4 bp per ion);
//   does not bind ssDNA or RNA. Signal is proportional to
//   amount of hybridized ds-143 on bead surface.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pelletForRu  = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
ruDrop1      = dispense 1 units of RuPhen3Cl2
ruDrop2      = dispense 1 units of RuPhen3Cl2

ruMerged     = mix ruDrop1 with ruDrop2 for 5s
ruLabelMix   = mix pelletForRu with ruMerged for 2m

// Magnetic separation: remove unbound Ru(Phen)3(2+).
heat ruLabelMix at 25c for 30s
dispose ruLabelMix

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: PBS wash x2 (remove excess Ru(Phen)3(2+)).
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "particles were washed two times with
//   2 droplets of PBS as in step 3."
//   Each wash: 1 unit PBS, mix 1m, magnet 30s, dispose.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// PBS Wash 1
pelletPW1  = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
pbsWash1   = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsMix1    = mix pelletPW1 with pbsWash1 for 1m
heat pbsMix1 at 25c for 30s
dispose pbsMix1

// PBS Wash 2
pelletPW2  = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
pbsWash2   = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsMix2    = mix pelletPW2 with pbsWash2 for 1m
heat pbsMix2 at 25c for 30s
dispose pbsMix2

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: TPA co-reactant addition.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "two droplets of TPA solution were
//   dispensed, merged, and delivered to the particles, where
//   they were re-suspended and mixed for 1 min."
//   TPA (tripropylamine) is the ECL co-reactant; oxidized
//   simultaneously with Ru(Phen)3(2+) at the ITO WE.
//   The TPA(+) radical reduces the luminophore to the
//   excited state that emits at ~610 nm.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pelletForTPA = dispense 1 units of MagneticParticles
tpaDrop1     = dispense 1 units of TPA
tpaDrop2     = dispense 1 units of TPA

tpaMerged    = mix tpaDrop1 with tpaDrop2 for 5s
finalDroplet = mix pelletForTPA with tpaMerged for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: ECL measurement.
//   Paper M&M Sec 2.3: "the final droplet containing TPA and
//   Ru(Phen)3(2+)-labeled DNA modified particles was actuated
//   to the ECL electrodes on the top-plate for ECL
//   measurements."
//   1.5 V DC applied between ITO WE and Ag/Au/ITO CE/RE
//   for 45 s. Maximum ECL counts recorded within first 10 s.
//   eclDetection module abstracts the PMT readout.
//   LOD: CLOD = 1.1 nM; absolute LOD = 1.5 femtomoles.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

eclSignal = detect eclDetection on finalDroplet for 45s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: ECL QC gate
// Pass (BB2): eclSignal > 0 -> ECL counts above blank
//             (hybridization detected); dispose final droplet.
// Fail (BB3): eclSignal <= 0 -> signal at or below blank
//             (no hybridization or below LOD); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (eclSignal > 0) {
    dispose finalDroplet
} else {
    drain finalDroplet
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose ECL signal droplet. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose eclSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
